WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:05.460
The Dark Knight has spoken, and he apparently
can't wait to get a look at the latest incarnation

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:07.460
of his most iconic foe.

00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:12.660
At this year's Toronto International Film
Festival, both Joaquin Phoenix's Joker and

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:17.440
Christian Bale's upcoming car racing biopic
Ford v Ferrari were screened.

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:22.939
Bale's latest film premiered mere hours before
Joker was shown at TIFF 2019, and Entertainment

00:00:22.939 --> 00:00:27.240
Tonight took the chance to get the former
Batman actor's take on Phoenix's Joker when

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:28.560
he walked the red carpet.

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:33.300
Like most of the world, Bale himself hadn't
yet seen Phoenix's work in Joker.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:37.620
He did, however, take the opportunity to throw
some love in Phoenix's general direction,

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:41.320
and note he finds it admirable that Phoenix
is following in the footsteps of the late

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:42.360
Heath Ledger.

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:46.860
"Joaquin is one of the best actors around,
you know, and obviously I worked with Heath,

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:51.060
and, you know, it's a brave thing to follow
up that performance."

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:55.880
Bale went on to say he thinks Phoenix "always
makes interesting choices" and he wished the

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:57.400
filmmakers the best with it.

00:00:57.580 --> 00:01:02.580
The world is also dying to see what maniacal
delights Phoenix and director Todd Phillips

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:05.160
have conjured with their standalone Joker
flick.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:10.100
According to most critics who caught the film
at TIFF, Phoenix and Phillips have redefined

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:15.360
the character for a new generation of Bat-fans,
delivering a gritty, wickedly insightful version

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:17.660
of the Joker the world didn't know it needed.

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:22.880
Many also agree that Joker could change audiences'
perception of what comic book movies can be

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:24.700
when it hits theaters this October.

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:28.560
As for Bale's kind words for Phoenix, they're
certainly high praise from an actor of his

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:29.440
stature.

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:33.700
Given Bale's past experience with the Clown
Prince of Crime, that praise is perhaps the

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:37.080
most meaningful kind Phoenix can receive for
playing the Joker.

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:41.500
Ledger's work with Bale in The Dark Knight
as the bullet-, gasoline-, and anarchy-loving

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:46.420
Joker truly is the stuff of legend; the brave
actor pushed the character beyond the frames

00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:50.580
of any comic book, film, or television version
of the Joker we'd seen before.

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:53.460
"If you're good at something, never do it
for free."

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:58.660
Purely from a legacy standpoint, most fans
believed the Joker would remain off-limits

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:04.060
indefinitely, with Ledger's performance continuing
to cast a long, dark shadow over the role.

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:07.600
But eight years passed before the Joker made
his big-screen return.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:13.100
The Clown Prince of Crime came back with Jared
Leto's wildly over-the-top take in the 2016

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:15.200
comic book misfire Suicide Squad.

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:19.760
While that movie does have its fans, Leto's
turn as the twisted gangster clown of Gotham

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:24.840
City ended up not exactly being what fans
were looking for in a big-screen Joker.

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:29.280
In the wake of the Suicide Squad debacle - and
with Cameron Monaghan delivering an equally

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:34.140
divisive version of the Joker on Fox's series
Gotham - many believed it would be an even

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:36.900
longer wait to see Joker in a feature film
again.

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:41.280
But then it was announced that Martin Scorsese
was helping to produce a standalone Joker

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:45.760
movie to be directed by Todd Phillips, who's
probably best known for The Hangover.

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:48.340
To most people, it was unexpected news.

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:50.820
"This isn't the real Caesar's Palace, is it?"

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:52.700
"What do you mean?"

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:57.360
"Did um...did Caesar live here?"

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:02.940
Scorsese left Joker during production to focus
on other projects, but his movies certainly

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:05.480
left their mark on the film Joker would become.

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:10.599
As news about the movie trickled out, it became
clear that Joker would spin an original take

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:14.220
on the character not beholden to any version
that came before.

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:18.820
After months of speculation about who would
claim the coveted role, Phoenix officially

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:23.599
boarded the project, an unexpected casting
choice leaving reason to believe that Joker

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:25.920
might actually turn into something special.

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:30.820
As Bale noted in his remarks to ET, it was
indeed "a brave thing" to follow in Ledger's

00:03:30.820 --> 00:03:34.740
clown-shoe-sized footsteps and bring Joker
back to the big screen.

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:39.220
Notably, Bale seemingly ignored Leto's take
on the character entirely.

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:41.700
"I don't want no beef."

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:43.480
"You don't want no beeeef?

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:44.640
You don't want no beef?

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:45.640
You don't want no beef…?"

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:50.840
If the largely positive early reviews are
any indication, Phoenix's bravery is more

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:51.820
than paying off.

00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:55.840
In fact, many are tapping Joker to be a major
player come awards season.

00:03:55.840 --> 00:04:00.400
Though Bale may soon be facing off against
the Joker for an Oscar instead of, you know,

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:05.920
the soul of Gotham, it appears Phoenix's Joker
already has a fan in the former Batman actor.

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:11.320
Phoenix's Joker is set to bring some chaos
to moviegoers on October 4, and Bale's Ford

00:04:11.320 --> 00:04:14.340
v Ferrari will race into theaters on November
15.

